A||||1||sdm1964||Headlights stay on||||13||
Z||000000||sdm1964||03-08-2000||09:01 PM||||Help, Only a few weeks till daytona and my car wants to go crazy on me.The drivers headlight was messing up, would not go up but would go down, the passenger light would go up but would not go down.A little help and it would go down. Now the headlights will not shut off, I have bought 2 switches, both good, no change. Un plug the fuse and put it back in and the lights stay off. It is only the headlights the exterior and dash lights will go out with the switch.Is there a  relay in the system i have not seen on the wiring schmatics? i found a broke wire at the relay with 2 pink and one red wire fixed those, unpluged them, still does the same thing. I think i am going crazy!!!!I work 10 hours a day, go to work in the dark and come home in the dark.I have worked 3 weeks strait with no day off and really need some help.<BR>TIA, Stephen||||reg||13
Z||000001||daved||03-08-2000||10:27 PM||||Stephen, you have nasty, multiple problems!<BR>There are many posts on this subject..try the search function....<BR>Lets see if I can help with a few of your problems.  <BR>Refer to Haynes, top of page 285 "Headlight Doors" schematic. The relay you repaired the wires on is the LH (drivers) actuator relay. If that relay is not energised for some reason,the door will still close, but will not open.  Faulty relay? Replace with the RH one and see if that fixes it. If not, then it most likely is the "Isolation Relay".<BR>Try the same swap for the RH (passenger) relay, but this side sounds like it's a motor problem (sorry).<BR> If your headlights wont go off, then it can only be the light switch not opening the circuit. While you were changing the light switch, the connector did not get turned around somehow?<BR> But you say if you pull the fuse and replace it, the headlights stay off!<BR>This cannot be wired as per the schematic. See Haynes, bottom of page 284 "Headlights" schematic. The symptoms suggest someone has added a relay to the headlight circuit, which is latching in.  With the headlights on, pull the fuse and listen for a tell-tale click to find this relay.  All I could suggest here is that you try to put the wiring back as was designed (impossible you say!), as to trouble-shoot non-standard wiring would be difficult......<BR>Best of luck, let us know how it goes, Dave||||reg||1
